 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A drone hit Saudi Arabia's tallest tower. Now its biggest port is threatened."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Eleven people were hurt on Tuesday when a drone hit the Public Investment Fund tower in Riyadh, Saudi civil defence says. It was the tower's second hit in a week. The Saudi-led coalition blames Yemen's Houthis and vows a firm response."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Then the coalition told civilians to leave Hodeidah port, its second warning in under a week. Houthi media reported strikes on the port soon after, with no casualties. Hodeidah is the main gateway for food into Houthi-held northern Yemen."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The Houthis answered. Their military spokesman says Jeddah and other Saudi Red Sea ports will become targets if Hodeidah is bombed. He told workers there to leave. The coalition says it also hit targets in Saada and Amran, near the border."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Houthis strike a Saudi Red Sea port before December? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
