 "upload": {
  "title": "Houthis Threaten Jeddah After Saudi Strikes on Hodeidah #shorts",
  "description": "On Tuesday, November 24, 2026, a drone hit the Public Investment Fund (PIF) tower in Riyadh's King Abdullah Financial District, Saudi Arabia's tallest skyscraper. Saudi civil defence said 11 people were injured (two Saudis, two Indians, three Nepalis and four Egyptians, per reports; the Indian embassy confirmed two Indian nationals were hurt). It was the second strike on the tower in about a week, after a November 19 missile damaged it. The Saudi-led coalition called the attack terrorist, blamed Yemen's Houthis and promised a firm response; the Houthis had not claimed Tuesday's strike in the reports we saw. Coalition spokesman Turki al-Maliki then posted a Joint Forces Command warning on X telling civilians to leave Hodeidah port, with a map of the area — its second evacuation call for the port in less than a week. Al Jazeera, citing the Houthi-run Saba news agency, reported that the coalition attacked the port shortly after; Houthi media reported no casualties. Hodeidah is the main port bringing food and other supplies into Houthi-controlled northern Yemen (Reuters). Houthi military spokesman Yahya Saree said Jeddah and all other Saudi ports on the Red Sea coast will become targets if Hodeidah is bombed, and urged employees, workers and shipping companies to leave those ports. The coalition also said it destroyed targets in the northern governorates of Saada and Amran near the Saudi border. Damage at Hodeidah has not been independently assessed; dates of individual strikes differ between reports. Locations on the map are approximate; lines show direction and distance, not flight paths.\n\nSources:\nAl Jazeera, Nov 24, 2026: 11 injured in Houthi drone attack on Riyadh tower, Saudi civil defence says\nAl Jazeera live, Nov 25, 2026: Saudi-led coalition strikes Yemen's Hodeidah port\nThe Tribune, Nov 25, 2026: Saudi-led coalition strikes Yemen's Hodeidah Port after Houthis threaten Red Sea ports\nTRT World, Nov 2026: Saudi-led coalition orders civilians to leave Yemen's Hodeidah port ahead of strikes\nThe Jerusalem Post, Nov 2026: Houthis threaten to attack Red Sea ports, Saudis issue warning\nU.S. News / Reuters, Nov 20, 2026: Saudi-Led Forces Strike Yemen Port as Houthis Warn Airlines off the Kingdom\nThe Brief, Nov 25, 2026: Saudi-led coalition orders civilians out of Hodeidah port as Houthis threaten Saudi Red Sea ports\n\n#geopolitics #SaudiArabia #Yemen #Houthis #RedSea #Jeddah",
